From aaa0215bb4ed7fbeb6b67f273ba631b818b3188c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:02:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] kboot: T6050: hand the GPU and the internal display over
 on 27.3 beta 1

The J714s needs the macOS 27.3 beta 1 stub (26C5035r, mBoot-20457.60.65.0.1) to boot all of
its cores, and the T6050 GPU and DCP handoffs only accepted 27.0.

- firmware: know 27.2 (mBoot-20457.41.3) and 27.3 beta 1 (<27 2 98 1>), as betizzel's m1n1
  for the J714s does.
- GPU: admit each build Linux's hw/t6050.rs identifies (27.0, 27.2, 27.3 beta 1): per build
  the 0x740/0x231 boot-filled records and the TEXT digest, from aurora-silicon/linux #1173
  (Rolando Trevino, rolotrealanis98). 27.0's digest and ranges are unchanged.
- DCP: accept 27.3 beta 1 beside 27.0, take its DCP image as the ADT names it (27.0 stays
  pinned), and publish apple,firmware-compat <27 3 0>, the key aurora-silicon/linux #1174
  chooses its 27.3 method table and swap layout by. dcpext engines must run the internal
  display's image. The compat idea follows TripleU613's J714s m1n1 (0004; betizzel,
  FatBoy721); its notch rows and display default (0006/0007) are not ported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/firmware.c              |  3 ++
 src/firmware.h              |  1 +
 src/kboot_display_handoff.c | 32 ++++++++++++------
 src/kboot_gpu.c             | 65 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 4 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

