From 313ad5ebcc3ef703dede80b38b6f6e1c35d1b38f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:17:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] kboot: T6050: PCIe: let an auto-PM storage domain gate
 itself during port bring-up

storage_check() stopped the GP bring-up when a storage power-state register changed outside its
actual-state and was-gated bits. APCIE_SYS_ST0 runs under auto power management (AUTO_ENABLE,
bit 28), and its hardware gates it while storage is idle: on a J714s (macOS 27.3 beta 1) it read
0x1f0003ff -> 0x1000030f after stage F, PS_AUTO (27:24) and the actual state both 0xf -> 0. The
check reported "storage changed after F" and left port 0, the N1 Wi-Fi, down (2 of 14 RAM test
boots on 2026-11-12). A domain with AUTO_ENABLE set before and after may now also move PS_AUTO; target,
auto-enable and every other bit still stop the bring-up, as do the ANS and NVMe checks after it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/pcie_t6050.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/pcie_t6050.c b/src/pcie_t6050.c
index 861b9959..f0bc22f3 100644
--- a/src/pcie_t6050.c
+++ b/src/pcie_t6050.c
@@ -350,8 +350,16 @@ static int storage_check(const char *tag, bool reference)
         printf("pcie-t6050: storage %s: 0x%lx 0x%08x -> 0x%08x\n", tag, storage_addr[i],
                storage_ref[i], cur[i]);
         changed++;
-        /* PS actual state and was-gated flags may move; target and auto must not */
-        if (i >= ST_PS && i < ST_SART && !((cur[i] ^ storage_ref[i]) & ~0x3f0))
+        /*
+         * PS actual state and was-gated flags may move; target and auto-enable must not. A
+         * domain under auto power management (AUTO_ENABLE, bit 28, set before and after) also
+         * moves its auto state (bits 27:24) on its own: on a J714s APCIE_SYS_ST0 went 0x1f0003ff
+         * -> 0x1000030f while the N1's link came up (storage idle, gated by the hardware).
+         */
+        u32 may_move = 0x3f0;
+        if (storage_ref[i] & cur[i] & BIT(28))
+            may_move |= 0x0f000000;
+        if (i >= ST_PS && i < ST_SART && !((cur[i] ^ storage_ref[i]) & ~may_move))
             continue;
         if (i >= ST_PS || i == ST_BOOT_STATUS || i == ST_CC)
             FAIL("storage changed %s\n", tag);
